/*  Four sensor logs averaged at once — and the two different ways a task goes wrong.

    Each task takes one station's raw readings, parses them, and returns the average. The
    stations are independent, so they run at the same time and the rabbit joins them all at
    `Done.`

    ★★ The point of the program is what happens when one of them cannot answer, because there
    are TWO answers and Cufet keeps them apart:

      - A reading that is not a number is a FAILURE the task chose to return. It rides in the
        type — the task's result is `number or failure` — and the await is refused unless it is
        handled. The station is reported as bad and the others carry on.

      - An empty log makes the average divide by zero. Nobody chose that; it is an EXCEPTION,
        and it travels to whoever awaits it. A `Try` at the await site catches it exactly as it
        would catch the same division written here.

    ⚠ The distinction is not a rule about tasks. `1 / 0` is an exception wherever it runs, and
    crossing a thread boundary does not turn it into a value. That is why the two arms below are
    `In case of failure` and `In case of exception` — the same two a sequential program uses.

    ★ Each task CATCHES its helper's failure and returns one of its own, rather than passing it
    outward. A task cannot propagate: `or pass the failure off` needs a declared fallible return
    type, and a task header declares nothing — it may hand back a result or merely send on a
    channel, and the line cannot say which. Catching and re-raising is the way across, and it
    costs nothing here because the message is worth rewriting anyway.
*/

Bind number or failure to average-of, given (the text raw):
    Define parts as raw split by ",".
    Define total as 0.
    Define count as 0.
    For each part in parts, repeat:
        Define trimmed-part as part trimmed.
        If the length of trimmed-part is not 0:
            Define value as trimmed-part converted to number.
            If value is void, return a failure "'{trimmed-part}' is not a reading" of category "parse".
            // ★ No `but void is` here: the guard above already narrowed `value` to a number,
            // and the checker refuses the redundant one rather than letting it read as caution.
            The total becomes total + value.
            Increment count by 1.
        Done.
    Done.
    // ⚠ NOT guarded, deliberately. An empty log is the exception half of this program: the
    // division below raises, the task ends, and the await is where it arrives.
    Return total / count.
Done.

Pull a rabbit.
    Have rabbit start a task as north:
        Try to:
            Return cast average-of on ("12, 14, 16").
        Done.
        In case of failure:
            Return a failure "{the message of the failure}" of category "parse".
        Done.
    Done.
    Have rabbit start a task as south:
        Try to:
            Return cast average-of on ("9, 11, warm, 13").
        Done.
        In case of failure:
            Return a failure "{the message of the failure}" of category "parse".
        Done.
    Done.
    Have rabbit start a task as east:
        Try to:
            Return cast average-of on ("20, 22").
        Done.
        In case of failure:
            Return a failure "{the message of the failure}" of category "parse".
        Done.
    Done.
    Have rabbit start a task as west:
        Try to:
            Return cast average-of on ("").
        Done.
        In case of failure:
            Return a failure "{the message of the failure}" of category "parse".
        Done.
    Done.

    State "station    average".

    // ★ Each await is wrapped once and handles both endings. The `Try` is what lets the loop of
    // stations continue past a station that could not answer — without it the first bad one ends
    // the program, which is the right default and the wrong thing here.
    Try to:
        State "north      {(the awaited result of north) converted to text}".
    Done.
    In case of failure:
        State "north      bad reading: {the message of the failure}".
    Done.
    In case of exception:
        State "north      no readings at all".
        Suppress the exception.
    Done.

    Try to:
        State "south      {(the awaited result of south) converted to text}".
    Done.
    In case of failure:
        State "south      bad reading: {the message of the failure}".
    Done.
    In case of exception:
        State "south      no readings at all".
        Suppress the exception.
    Done.

    Try to:
        State "east       {(the awaited result of east) converted to text}".
    Done.
    In case of failure:
        State "east       bad reading: {the message of the failure}".
    Done.
    In case of exception:
        State "east       no readings at all".
        Suppress the exception.
    Done.

    Try to:
        State "west       {(the awaited result of west) converted to text}".
    Done.
    In case of failure:
        State "west       bad reading: {the message of the failure}".
    Done.
    In case of exception:
        State "west       no readings at all".
        Suppress the exception.
    Done.

    // ★ Every station was awaited, so every ending was claimed by the code above. The rabbit's
    // `Done.` has nothing left to report — a fault reaches it only when nobody read the result.
    State "all four stations accounted for".
Done.
